  "body": "Stacked on #809\n\nFork synced at v0.17.0. The branch is cut from #809's head (`issue/789-workholding-accessories`, 9d8c7fa1), which carries #802. Only the last commit (b480ae81) belongs to this PR.\n\n## What changed\n- **Lenient `vise` / `accessory` keys (#812 item 1).** `FixtureDto` now holds both keys as raw JSON, as #823 does for `plate` / `on_plate`. The new `project::fixture_keys` reads each key into its typed form. A key that doesn't parse (an unknown accessory `kind`, a vise shape this build can't read, a mistyped figure) or that breaks its law is dropped on its own. The fixture keeps its saved facets as plain steel, and the rest of the file loads.\n  - **Load notes.** Each drop is a load note that names the fixture, the key and the serde or law reason. `open_noted` logs it, and the GUI's open shows it on the status line. Previously a law-breaking key was only logged.\n  - **Checks moved to the loader.** `ViseDto::to_params` now returns the parameters unchecked, and the loader checks them. `accessory::checked_on_load` is gone.\n  - **Wire format.** Unchanged.\n- **A stud as wide as its strap, or wider, is refused by name (item 2).** The refusal reads \"Strap clamp stud diameter … must be less than the strap width …\". It comes from `Accessory::check`, so `InsertAccessory` and `SetAccessory` both refuse the stud when the command is created. #809's `every_kind_builds_closed_shells…` used to build a 40 mm stud through the 31.75 mm strap; it now asserts the refusal.\n- **Parallels-fit dialog (items 3 and 4).** In fit mode the height row reads \"Height (set by the fit)\" and is disabled. A hint says that the fit keeps the stock where it is and drops the vise, so a stock resting on the vise floor takes the vise below the table.\n- **Decisions:** `docs/decisions/812-lenient-fixture-keys.md`.\n\n## How tested\n- `crates/app/tests/fixture_keys_lenient.rs` (new):\n  - `unknown_or_malformed_fixture_keys_are_dropped_with_a_note_and_the_load_goes_on`: a file with a vise key in an unknown `hydraulic` shape, an accessory of unknown kind `vacuum_pod`, and a soft jaw whose `height` is `\"tall\"`. The file loads with exactly three notes, each naming its fixture and key. Those fixtures stay as plain steel with their facets, and a good vise and a good clamp in the same file are untouched. A clean file gives no notes.\n  - `a_law_breaking_accessory_key_is_noted_too`\n  - `a_stud_wider_than_its_strap_is_refused_by_name`: covers both `InsertAccessory` and `SetAccessory`.\n- `camcraft-ui` `fixture_accessory_tests::the_fit_says_it_sinks_the_vise_and_holds_the_height`: structural, kittest, no pixels. The fit label is present and disabled, and the plain \"Height\" row is absent. The sink hint is shown, and both the label and the hint go when fit mode is off.\n- Re-run and green locally (macOS):\n  - app: `builtin_vise` (its nonsense-key log test still passes through the note's log line), `builtin_accessory`, `accessory_collisions`, `mcp_accessory`, `mcp_vise`\n  - ui: `--lib fixture` (31 tests, CWD `crates/ui`)\n  - `cargo clippy -p camcraft-app -p camcraft-ui --all-targets -D warnings`\n- Linux quick gate: result posted as a PR comment.\n\n## Not exercised\n- Opening a hand-edited file in the GUI to read the status line. The note path is the same `load_noted` one that #342's notes already use.\n- #823's plate keys still only log: #823 isn't in this stack. Once both PRs merge, `plate_dto::link_from` can route through `fixture_keys` so the plate drops also reach the notes.\n- #811 puts its `self_centering` key inside `ViseDto`, so that key gets the lenient read automatically. When #811 merges main, it only needs to apply its `style` field to the unchecked `to_params` (a likely small conflict in `vise_dto.rs`).\n- The #811 review items on #812 aren't in #809's code and are left for their own PR:\n  - the dovetail lip hint\n  - a \"Centre on stock\" action\n  - the absolute 1e-6 mm `CENTRE_TOL`\n\nChangelog: A fixture's vise or accessory key that this build can't read (an unknown kind or a bad shape) is dropped with a load note, and the project still opens. A strap clamp's stud must be narrower than its strap. The parallels fit marks its height as set by the fit and warns that the vise drops below the table (#812)\n\nEffort: high (no escalation)\n\nFixes #812\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nhttps://claude.ai/code/session_01CUsqDAAAJyAPrC37zBzbbX\n",
